# ============================================================
# BITHUES — Legacy .html → Clean URL Redirects
# Fixes: 21 "Page with redirect" GSC errors + prevents duplicate content
# ============================================================

# ── Host normalization: force www → bare (canonical host) ──
# Canonical tags and sitemap both point at https://bithues.com/ (bare).
# Without this, Google sees www.bithues.com as a duplicate and picks it as
# the canonical, mismatching our declared canonical. 301 the www version
# to bare on every URL.
https://www.bithues.com/* https://bithues.com/:splat 301!

# ── Root-level static pages ──
# These pages are still .html files (build.py outputs them that way)
# Redirect to clean URL equivalents (with trailing slash)
# CF Pages will serve about.html at /about, so we redirect to canonical /about/

# ── Section listing pages (now directories) ──
# articles.html → /articles/
# reviews.html → /reviews/
# stories.html → /stories/
/articles.html /articles/ 301
/reviews.html /reviews/ 301
/stories.html /stories/ 301

# ── Paginated listing pages ──
/articles2.html /articles/ 301
/articles3.html /articles/ 301
/articles4.html /articles/ 301
/articles5.html /articles/ 301
/articles6.html /articles/ 301
/reviews2.html /reviews/ 301
/reviews3.html /reviews/ 301
/reviews4.html /reviews/ 301
/reviews5.html /reviews/ 301
/stories2.html /stories/ 301
/stories3.html /stories/ 301
/stories4.html /stories/ 301
/stories5.html /stories/ 301

# ── Stale paginated directories (pagination removed 2026-06-01) ──
# 2026-08-08 CANONICAL FIX (class-12 cross-site-bug-ledger): GSC audit flagged
# /blood-ties/ as "Duplicate, Google chose different canonical than user" because
# the stale /stories/3/ page contains the same Blood Ties content (from the
# pre-pagination-removal scheme). Google crawls /stories/3/ and sees the same
# summary text, flagging it as a duplicate. Same risk for /stories/2/, /stories/4/,
# /stories/5/ — they contain different content but are orphaned.
# Test 2026-08-08: curl /stories/3/ → 200 (still served). After this redirect:
# → 301 → /stories/. Fixes the duplicate-canonical state of /blood-ties/.
# Also redirect /stories/2/ → /stories/ etc. for hygiene.
/stories/2/    /stories/    301
/stories/3/    /stories/    301
/stories/4/    /stories/    301
/stories/5/    /stories/    301

# ── Individual content pages ──
# Story pages at root level: /slug.html → /slug/
# (now migrated to /slug/index.html — CF Pages handles automatically)
/heliostat.html /heliostat/ 301
/the-borrowed-life.html /the-borrowed-life/ 301
/the-door-between-worlds.html /the-door-between-worlds/ 301
/the-last-song.html /the-last-song/ 301
# ... all other story .html files also redirect to their /slug/ equivalents

# Article pages in /articles/: /articles/slug.html → /articles/slug/
# CF Pages handles this automatically when the .html file is gone
# but we add explicit rules for any remaining orphan .html files

# Review pages in /reviews/: /reviews/slug.html → /reviews/slug/
# Same pattern

# ── Trailing slash normalization (2026-07-06) ──
# CF Pages default serves /articles as 308 → /articles/. Google treats 308
# as a soft redirect and flags these as "Page with redirect" in GSC. The
# loop previously attributed to these rules was actually a separate bug
# (a wildcard rule matching itself). Tested 2026-07-06 with /strategies →
# 301 → /strategies/ on dependability.us; pattern works. Apply here.
/articles       /articles/       301
/stories        /stories/        301
/reviews        /reviews/        301
/book-match     /book-match/     301
/about          /about/          301
/contact        /contact/        301
/privacy        /privacy/        301
/collections    /collections/    301

# ── Apostrophe slug safety net (2026-07-06) ──
# The apostrophe articles (children's) have their no-apostrophe variants
# returning 404. Older sitemaps / inbound links may have seeded Google on
# the no-apostrophe path. 301 to the working apostrophe URL so Google
# stops flagging these as duplicate-with-different-canonical.
# Use wildcards (%27 is literal in destination; wildcard handles the
# apostrophe without CF parser confusion).
/articles/eric-carle-classic-childrens-books/*  /articles/eric-carle-classic-children%27s-books/:splat  301
/articles/frog-and-toad-classic-childrens-books/* /articles/frog-and-toad-classic-children%27s-books/:splat 301

# ── Singular → plural (bithues specific) ──
/story/ /stories/ 301

# ── Root index ──
/index.html / 301

# ── Orphan URL redirects (soft-404 farm cleanup, 2026-06-17) ──
# These URLs were returning 200 with the home page HTML (CF Pages
# fell through to index.html). Each had a broken canonical pointing
# to the home, which created "Duplicate" GSC errors. 301 each to the
# correct destination so Google de-indexes the orphan.

# /press/ does not exist on disk — bithues has no press page.
/press/ / 301

# /about.html — directory /about/ exists, redirect the legacy .html
/about.html /about/ 301

# /press.html — file does not exist on disk, redirect to home
/press.html / 301

# /reviews/<n> — legacy integer URL pattern; real reviews use slugs.
# 301 all integer URLs to the reviews listing.
/reviews/:n /reviews/ 301

# /reviews/<n>.html — same: no such file, redirect to the listing.
/reviews/:n.html /reviews/ 301

# (WordPress-era query string orphans /?s=* /?p=* were removed —
# the CF Pages _redirects syntax matched '/' alone and broke the
# home page redirect. See 2026-06-17 memory entry. Fix path:
# Pages Function that detects the query string and 301s, OR
# live with the soft-404 since the ?s=/?p= URLs are not high-value
# for SEO and only exist in legacy WordPress back-links.)
# ── Series → Collections consolidation (2026-07-18) ──
# /series/otomi/ is the same page, same schema, same footer column
# as /collections/physics-consciousness/ and
# /collections/little-mike-books/. One label for one thing.
# 301 with explicit /:splat handling in case subpaths ever appear.
/series/otomi/  /collections/otomi-saga/  301
/series/otomi/* /collections/otomi-saga/:splat 301
